SUMMARY:Adair’s Cajun Cooking 🦞 🦐 
DESCRIPTION:Senior Singles Fun Bunch\n**Adair’s Cajun Cooking is now loc
 ated permanently (instead of only having a food truck) in a brick-and-mort
 ar location in downtown Hendersonville. They are in the basement at 321 N.
  Main St. Ste C. There will be Spanish moss-covered wood decor out front w
 ith a life-size alligator sculpture. Hard to miss! 🐊**\n\n**They offer 
 authentic Cajun food since the owners are from Louisiana. Some of their di
 shes are crawfish or shrimp etouffee\, 🦐 chicken & sausage gumbo\, jamb
 alaya\, and red beans & rice to name a few. And if you have a sweet tooth 
 🦷 they offer pecan pralines and bread pudding. 😋 To see more of thei
 r menu just google Adair’s Cajun Cooking menu.**\n\n**For now they are c
 ounter service only (they just opened in April) with dining in and also th
 ere is outdoor seating.**\n\n**Dogs are allowed in the outdoor seating are
 a only. 🐶**\n\n**Come join me for some good ole Cajun food! 😋**\n\n*
 *RESERVATIONS: Adair’s usually does not do reservations\, but for our gr
 oup they are!! Yay!! Reservations at 6:00 PM.**\n\n**Questions?**\n\n**Sha
 e ~ (828)699-8180 I prefer text since I work\, but I will answer calls whe
 n I can.**\n\n**Email: Shae.kemerer@aol.com**
