DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260811T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260811T203000
SUMMARY:Come sing with us! Vocal workshop and rehearsal - Land Of The Sky 
 Chorus
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Area A Cappella Singers\nWhether you are an experien
 ced singer\, or just like to sing in your car\, come join us as our guest!
  The Land of The Sky Chorus\, located in Asheville\, NC\, is welcoming gue
 sts - men and women - who are interested in joining us in the world-wide c
 ommunity of a cappella singing.\n\nNo experience is required\; we provide 
 music\, voice training and an enjoyable singing experience under expert le
 adership. Our repertoire of music is fun and spans many styles - most song
 s are easy to learn and sing. Learning materials are provided to help you 
 get started\, and you will be paired with a singing "Buddy" so you can joi
 n in right away.\n\nWe will be here to greet you as early as 6:15pm to hel
 p you get situated.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/asheville-area-a-cappella-singers/eve
 nts/jztwvtyjclbpb/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260202T005102Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260202T005102Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Asheville Classic Books Meetup Group": "https://www.meetup.com/asheville-classic-books-meetup-group/events/314557384/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_asheville_classic_books_meetup_group
X-SOURCE:Books That Age Like Wine
UID:event_314557384@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260717T031309Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260811T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260811T203000
SUMMARY:The Hearing Trumpet by Leonora Carrington
DESCRIPTION:Books That Age Like Wine\nAn old woman enters into a fantastic
 al world of dreams and nightmares in this surrealist classic admired by Bj
 örk and Luis Buñuel.\n\nLeonora Carrington\, painter\, playwright\, and 
 novelist\, was a surrealist trickster par excellence\, and The Hearing Tru
 mpet is the witty\, celebratory key to her anarchic and allusive body of w
 ork. The novel begins in the bourgeois comfort of a residential corner of 
 a Mexican city and ends with a man-made apocalypse that promises to usher 
 in the earth’s rebirth. In between we are swept off to a most curious ol
 d-age home run by a self-improvement cult and drawn several centuries back
  in time with a cross-dressing Abbess who is on a quest to restore the Hol
 y Grail to its rightful owner\, the Goddess Venus. Guiding us is one of th
 e most unexpected heroines in twentieth-century literature\, a nonagenaria
 n vegetarian named Marian Leatherby\, who\, as Olga Tokarczuk writes in he
 r afterword\, is “hard of hearing” but “full of life.”
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/asheville-classic-books-meetup-group/
 events/314557384/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260430T103510Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260430T103510Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
