DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260908T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260908T203000
SUMMARY:Come sing with us! Vocal workshop and rehearsal - Land Of The Sky 
 Chorus
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Area A Cappella Singers\nWhether you are an experien
 ced singer\, or just like to sing in your car\, come join us as our guest!
  The Land of The Sky Chorus\, located in Asheville\, NC\, is welcoming gue
 sts - men and women - who are interested in joining us in the world-wide c
 ommunity of a cappella singing.\n\nNo experience is required\; we provide 
 music\, voice training and an enjoyable singing experience under expert le
 adership. Our repertoire of music is fun and spans many styles - most song
 s are easy to learn and sing. Learning materials are provided to help you 
 get started\, and you will be paired with a singing "Buddy" so you can joi
 n in right away.\n\nWe will be here to greet you as early as 6:15pm to hel
 p you get situated.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/asheville-area-a-cappella-singers/eve
 nts/jztwvtyjcmblb/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260202T005102Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260202T005102Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Asheville Classic Books Meetup Group": "https://www.meetup.com/asheville-classic-books-meetup-group/events/314577908/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_asheville_classic_books_meetup_group
X-SOURCE:Books That Age Like Wine
UID:event_314577908@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260717T031309Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260908T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260908T203000
SUMMARY:The Forsyte Saga - Volume 1 - \nJohn Galsworthy
DESCRIPTION:Books That Age Like Wine\nWe will only be reading “The Man o
 f Property” but we can stay later and discuss the other two volumes if a
 nyone is interested..\n\nThe three novels which make up The Forsyte Saga c
 hronicle the ebbing social power of the commercial upper-middle class Fors
 yte family between 1886 and 1920. Galsworthy's masterly narrative examines
  not only their fortunes but also the wider developments within society\, 
 particularly the changing position of women. This is the only critical edi
 tion of the work available\, with Notes that explain contemporary artistic
  and literary allusions and define the slang of the time.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/asheville-classic-books-meetup-group/
